<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huáscar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1503–<a href="/years/1532">1532</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Waskar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Huáscar was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sapa-inca">Sapa Inca</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca Empire</a> from about 1527 to 1532, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cuzco</a> after the death of his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huayna-capac">Huayna Capac</a>. His half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atahualpa">Atahualpa</a>, based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a>, rose against him, and in the civil war that followed Atahualpa's generals defeated and captured Huáscar in 1532. He was killed on Atahualpa's orders while Atahualpa was a prisoner of the Spanish.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/huascar.jpg" alt="Huáscar" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Waskhar_portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
